# Data Fetching

- Use the shared `api` client from `src/lib/api-client.ts` for HTTP requests.
- Build feature-local query and mutation modules in `src/features/<feature>/api/`.
- Use `queryOptions`, `useQuery`, and `useMutation` from TanStack Query; keep query keys scoped to the feature and include every parameter that changes the result.
- Mutation hooks own only domain-wide effects: scoped invalidation, cache writes, and auth-state cleanup. Forward `onSuccess`, `onError`, and `onSettled` to caller configs.
- Keep view-local behavior at the call site: dialog closes, form resets, edit-mode toggles, navigation, and action-specific toasts.
- The shared API client already handles standard HTTP error toasts, so avoid duplicating them in components.
- In `src/lib/auth.tsx`, keep credential persistence and session refresh logic centralized instead of duplicating it in components.
- Route loaders that prefetch data should reuse the query options factory so loaders and components share the same query key.
